Interactive Single Sign-On (SSO) and SCIM provisioning for OPNsense.

Adds OpenID Connect (OIDC), SAML 2.0 and JWT forward-auth as authentication
types under System > Access > Servers. OPNsense acts as a pure Relying Party /
Service Provider: MFA and passkeys live at the Identity Provider
(Authentik, Keycloak, Entra ID, Zitadel, ...).

Features:
  * WebGUI login via an SSO button on the login page (OIDC, SAML and JWT).
  * Captive Portal login via OIDC/SAML.
  * OpenVPN login via the deferred web flow (WEB_AUTH / pending auth).
  * JWT forward-auth: trust a signed JWT from a trusted upstream proxy,
    gated to the proxy's source IP (verified signature, iss/aud/exp).
  * OIDC client authentication without a shared secret if you need it:
    client_secret_jwt, private_key_jwt (we serve the public JWKS) or mutual TLS.
    The IdP's MFA context (acr) and re-authentication age (max_age) are checked
    on the way back, not merely requested.
  * IdP group -> OPNsense group mapping (privileges resolved by the ACL),
    nested claims and Entra ID group-overage included.
  * SCIM 2.0 provisioning: the IdP pushes account creations, updates and
    deactivations, so a revoked user is disabled - and their open sessions
    ended - when the directory says so, rather than at their next login
    attempt. Bearer token plus source-address gated. It never touches a
    privileged account or one owning a local password, and a SCIM delete
    deactivates instead of removing.

The local password path (+ native TOTP) stays active as break-glass.
